schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Verra blocked Toucan's tokenization of retired carbon credits (May 2022)
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Toucan Protocol moved carbon credits onto the blockchain so they could be
    traded openly, but in May 2022 Verra, the world's largest carbon-credit
    registry, ruled that the specific credits being used (already-retired
    ones) should not be tokenized that way, and blocked the practice.
  evidence: >-
    Cited to "Toucan: Response to Verra's announcement" (blog.toucan.earth) in
    the article's References — Toucan's own account of the decision.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/what-web3-can-cant-do.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the article's central cautionary tale for "a blockchain cannot
    verify the real world for you" — the code executed correctly, but the
    off-chain registry/rules layer around the carbon credits did not
    cooperate, illustrating that tokenization does not resolve underlying
    real-world governance disputes.
  uncertainty: >-
    High-risk MRV/carbon-market claim per the ingest skill's high-risk
    triggers. Sourced only to Toucan's own response post (a party to the
    dispute), not to Verra's original ruling directly; the article does not
    cite Verra's own statement. Treat as one side's framing of a contested
    registry decision until cross-checked against Verra's own published policy.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  high_risk: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/what-web3-can-cant-do.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
